  "sn12.32:14.8": "",
  "sn12.32:14.9": "Variants for <i lang='pi' translate='no'>nānussavanti</i> are from the roots <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sav</i> (“flow”) and <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sī</i> (“lie”). Pali often couples verbs and nouns from the same root for emphasis, and this is probably the case here, “defilements don’t defile”. ",
  "sn12.32:14.10": "",
  "sn12.32:15.1": "",
  "sn12.32:15.2": "",
  "sn12.32:15.3": "“The ascetic” is the Buddha. ",
  "sn12.32:15.4": "",
  "sn12.32:15.5": "",
  "sn12.32:16.1": "",
  "sn12.32:16.2": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Pubbe appaṭisaṁviditaṁ</i> is an idiom elsewhere used when visiting someone “without letting them know beforehand” (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn91/en/sujato#26.4'>MN 91:26.4</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.50/en/sujato#4.7'>AN 5.50:4.7</a>). ",
